WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.680
A control implementation narrative explains how the cloud service satisfies a security

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.020
expectation.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.960
It should identify what the control means for this specific system, where it applies,

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:14.940
who owns it, how it operates, how effectiveness is demonstrated,

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.840
and what evidence supports it.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.860
The narrative is the bridge between control language and the real architecture, process,

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.760
tool, or workflow.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.980
Responsibility needs to be explicit.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.200
A control may be provider-managed, customer-managed, shared,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.820
or inherited from another system or platform.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.360
Some controls may have multiple layers.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.340
For example, a platform may provide logging capability,

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.880
the provider may configure application logging,

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.820
and the customer may review tenant-specific events.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.360
A good narrative explains the split without hiding uncertainty or pushing responsibility

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.100
into vague language.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.560
Control narratives should be specific enough for assessment but maintainable over time.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.860
Overly generic statements do not help reviewers understand the system.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.080
Overly brittle statements can become outdated after routine engineering changes.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.500
The best narratives describe stable mechanisms, ownership, evidence sources,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:14.520
and operating expectations while avoiding unnecessary details that will churn constantly.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.700
They tell reviewers what matters and where to verify it.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.640
Copy-paste control language is weak documentation because it repeats the requirement

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.780
without explaining implementation.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.240
A reviewer should not have to infer how the control works from a restated sentence.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:33.540
Strong narratives describe the actual service, the actual process,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.520
and the actual evidence.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.620
They also acknowledge exceptions, limitations, and inherited responsibilities.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:44.040
Honest specificity is more credible than broad claims.
